THE CASE AGAINST THE TARGET:
The 'Schema-First' mechanism assumes that defining a schema causally prevents 'unstructured noise,' but it fails to account for the causal reality of exploratory research where the variables themselves are unknown until an experiment runs. By enforcing a schema gatekeeper *before* logging, the mechanism causally blocks the recording of novel findings that do not fit the pre-existing contract, effectively blinding the team to the very anomalies they are researching. The mechanism protects structure at the cost of suppressing the causal discovery process.

